## 8. GO-TO-MARKET STRATEGY

### Phase 1 — Uzbekistan Beachhead (Months 1–3)
- Target: Restaurants, salons, retail shops in Tashkent
- Channel: Direct outreach to business owners (founder-led sales)
- Offer: Free onboarding, help them set everything up personally
- Goal: 10 paid customers, collect testimonials and case studies
- Leverage: Founder's existing local network and prior experience helping a local business

### Phase 2 — Content-Led Growth (Months 3–6)
- Build in public: Document the platform being built on social media
- Create content showing before/after for local businesses using the platform
- Uzbek/Russian-language YouTube, TikTok, Telegram channel tutorials
- Partner with local business communities, co-working spaces, chambers of commerce

### Phase 3 — CIS Expansion (Months 6–12)
- Translate fully to Russian
- Target Kazakhstan, Azerbaijan, Georgia
- Explore partnerships with local business associations

### Distribution Risks & Mitigations
> *"Distribution and getting users"* — Founder's #1 concern. Rightfully so.

- **Risk:** Building a great product nobody finds
- **Mitigation:** Do not wait for product to be perfect. Get 5 real users during build. Let them shape the product. Their word of mouth is worth more than any ad.
- **Mitigation:** Founder becomes the face of the brand on social media. Document the journey. This is free distribution.
- **Mitigation:** Give the free tier genuine value. A business that got a free logo, Google profile, and Instagram setup will tell other business owners.

